      "before": "256 threads per CTA, one-CTA-per-SM launch bound; one 207,232-byte dynamic smem allocation (storage account plus 256-byte slack) against the 232,448-byte device max minus ~1 KiB static; ~208 registers per thread without spilling",
      "after": "256 threads per CTA with __launch_bounds__(256, 1); one 207,232-byte dynamic smem request including 256-byte slack, checked against the runtime device opt-in maximum"
    },
    {
      "path": "root.yaml.REALIZATION.Require[2].Reason",
      "before": "The Tile_pipeline account and the register-resident fragment and accumulator design assume exactly this residency and budget; an over-budget launch is rejected at the check rather than silently mis-laid-out",
      "after": "The shared-memory request must cover the Tile_pipeline storage layout; run_cfg checks it against the device opt-in limit before launch; the registered arrays do not establish compiled register allocation or spilling"
