    {
      "path": "split_kv.yaml.REALIZATION.Require[2].Reason",
      "before": "A separate 32,768-byte query tile would need 235,456 bytes against a 231,424-byte budget, so the tile trades it for 128 registers of cached A fragments per thread on top of 64 accumulator registers; the slot-0 release barrier is what makes the reuse safe",
      "after": "A separate 32,768-byte query tile would need 235,456 bytes against a 231,424-byte layout budget; cached A fragments and accumulators instead hold 128 and 64 32-bit slots per thread, without determining compiled register allocation; the slot-0 release barrier makes reuse safe"
    },
    {
      "path": "split_kv.yaml.REALIZATION.Require[6].Choice",
      "before": "512 threads per CTA under a two-blocks-per-SM launch bound, i.e. 64 registers per thread, a 9,776-byte static shared block and no dynamic shared memory; four segment-groups of 128 threads each own one float4 of the 512 latent columns",
